# Cloud-Based Browser DAW — Full Architecture & Implementation Plan

## Overview

Build **SoundForge Studio**, a professional browser-based Digital Audio Workstation where users can create, edit, mix, and collaborate on music projects entirely in the browser. The system must support real-time audio playback, multi-track editing, plugin processing, collaborative sessions, and an AI music assistant.

---

## 1. High-Level Architecture

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph Client["Browser Client (Next.js + TailwindCSS)"]
        UI["React UI Layer"]
        DAW["DAW Editor (Canvas/WebGL)"]
        AE["Audio Engine (Web Audio API + AudioWorklets)"]
        COLLAB_C["Collaboration Client (WebSocket)"]
        IDB["IndexedDB Local Cache"]
        PLUGIN_H["Plugin Host (WASM Sandbox)"]
        AI_C["AI Assistant Client"]
    end

    subgraph API["API Gateway (Node.js / Express)"]
        AUTH["Auth Service (JWT + OAuth)"]
        PROJ["Project Service"]
        STORE["Storage Service"]
        COLLAB_S["Collaboration Service (WebSocket)"]
        AI_S["AI Music Service"]
        PLUGIN_R["Plugin Registry"]
    end

    subgraph Data["Data Layer"]
        PG["PostgreSQL (Users, Projects, Metadata)"]
        REDIS["Redis (Sessions, Pub/Sub, CRDT Sync)"]
        S3["Object Storage / S3 (Audio Files)"]
        VECTOR["Vector DB (AI Embeddings)"]
    end

    UI --> AUTH
    UI --> PROJ
    UI --> STORE
    DAW --> AE
    DAW --> COLLAB_C
    COLLAB_C --> COLLAB_S
    AE --> PLUGIN_H
    AE --> IDB
    AI_C --> AI_S

    AUTH --> PG
    PROJ --> PG
    STORE --> S3
    COLLAB_S --> REDIS
    AI_S --> VECTOR
```

---

## 2. Technology Stack

| Layer | Technology | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| **Frontend** | Next.js 14 (App Router) | SSR for landing pages, client-side for DAW editor |
| **Styling** | TailwindCSS 3 | Rapid, consistent UI with dark-mode support |
| **Audio** | Web Audio API + AudioWorklets | Low-latency, real-time DSP on audio thread |
| **Rendering** | HTML Canvas (waveforms) + WebGL (spectrogram, meters) | GPU-accelerated visualization |
| **State** | Zustand | Lightweight, minimal boilerplate for DAW state |
| **Backend** | Node.js + Express | Non-blocking I/O, WebSocket native support |
| **Real-time** | Socket.IO (WebSocket) | Built-in rooms, reconnection, fallbacks |
| **Database** | PostgreSQL (Prisma ORM) | Relational data: users, projects, tracks, permissions |
| **Cache/PubSub** | Redis | Session store, collaboration pub/sub, rate limiting |
| **Object Storage** | S3-compatible (AWS S3 / MinIO) | Audio file blobs, stems, exports |
| **Local Cache** | IndexedDB (via Dexie.js) | Offline project cache, undo history |
| **AI** | OpenAI API / Replicate (MusicGen) | Chord suggestion, stem separation, generation |
| **Auth** | NextAuth.js (OAuth + credentials) | Google/GitHub/email login, JWT sessions |

---

## 3. Core Systems Design

### 3.1 Authentication & User Accounts

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant C as Client
    participant A as Auth Service
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    U->>C: Click "Sign in with Google"
    C->>A: POST /api/auth/signin (OAuth)
    A->>A: Validate OAuth token
    A->>DB: Upsert user record
    A-->>C: JWT access + refresh tokens
    C->>C: Store JWT in httpOnly cookie
    C->>A: GET /api/me (with JWT)
    A-->>C: User profile + subscription tier
```

**Key decisions:**
- **NextAuth.js** handles OAuth (Google, GitHub) and email/password
- JWT stored in `httpOnly` cookies (XSS resistant)
- Refresh token rotation with 15-min access token TTL
- Subscription tiers: Free (3 projects, 100 MB), Pro ($12/mo, unlimited), Team ($25/seat/mo)

**Data model:**
```sql
CREATE TABLE users (
    id            UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    email         VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    name          VARCHAR(255),
    avatar_url    TEXT,
    password_hash TEXT,  -- NULL for OAuth-only users
    provider      VARCHAR(50),  -- 'google', 'github', 'credentials'
    subscription  VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT 'free',
    storage_used  BIGINT DEFAULT 0,
    created_at    TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at    TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

---

### 3.2 Project Management System

**Data model:**
```sql
CREATE TABLE projects (
    id          UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    owner_id    UUID REFERENCES users(id),
    title       VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    description TEXT,
    bpm         INT DEFAULT 120,
    time_sig    VARCHAR(10) DEFAULT '4/4',
    sample_rate INT DEFAULT 44100,
    is_public   BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
    version     INT DEFAULT 1,
    created_at  TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at  TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE TABLE tracks (
    id          UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    project_id  UUID REFERENCES projects(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    name        VARCHAR(255),
    type        VARCHAR(20),  -- 'audio', 'midi', 'bus', 'master'
    color       VARCHAR(7),
    volume      FLOAT DEFAULT 0.8,
    pan         FLOAT DEFAULT 0.0,
    muted       BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
    solo        BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
    sort_order  INT DEFAULT 0,
    created_at  TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE TABLE clips (
    id          UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    track_id    UUID REFERENCES tracks(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    name        VARCHAR(255),
    type        VARCHAR(20),  -- 'audio', 'midi'
    start_time  FLOAT NOT NULL,  -- in beats
    duration    FLOAT NOT NULL,  -- in beats
    offset      FLOAT DEFAULT 0, -- source offset
    gain        FLOAT DEFAULT 1.0,
    fade_in     FLOAT DEFAULT 0,
    fade_out    FLOAT DEFAULT 0,
    audio_url   TEXT,            -- S3 key for audio clips
    midi_data   JSONB,           -- note events for MIDI clips
    created_at  TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE TABLE project_collaborators (
    project_id  UUID REFERENCES projects(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    user_id     UUID REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    role        VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT 'editor',  -- 'viewer', 'editor', 'admin'
    joined_at   TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),
    PRIMARY KEY (project_id, user_id)
);
```

**REST API surface:**

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| `GET` | `/api/projects` | List user's projects |
| `POST` | `/api/projects` | Create new project |
| `GET` | `/api/projects/:id` | Get project with tracks + clips |
| `PUT` | `/api/projects/:id` | Update project metadata |
| `DELETE` | `/api/projects/:id` | Delete project |
| `POST` | `/api/projects/:id/tracks` | Add track |
| `PUT` | `/api/projects/:id/tracks/:tid` | Update track |
| `DELETE` | `/api/projects/:id/tracks/:tid` | Delete track |
| `POST` | `/api/projects/:id/tracks/:tid/clips` | Add clip |
| `PUT` | `/api/projects/:id/clips/:cid` | Update clip |
| `DELETE` | `/api/projects/:id/clips/:cid` | Delete clip |
| `POST` | `/api/projects/:id/collaborators` | Invite collaborator |
| `POST` | `/api/projects/:id/export` | Export mixdown |

