### 3.3 Cloud Storage

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph Upload Flow
        C[Client] -->|multipart/form-data| API[API Server]
        API -->|presigned URL| S3[S3 Bucket]
        API -->|metadata| PG[PostgreSQL]
    end

    subgraph Download Flow
        C2[Client] -->|GET /api/files/:id| API2[API Server]
        API2 -->|signed URL (1hr TTL)| C2
        C2 -->|fetch| S3_2[S3 CDN]
    end
```

**Strategy:**
- **Upload:** Client requests a presigned S3 URL from the API; uploads directly to S3 (no server bottleneck)
- **Download:** API generates signed URLs with 1-hour TTL; streamed via CloudFront CDN
- **Local cache:** Dexie.js IndexedDB stores recently used audio blobs for offline work
- **File organization:** `s3://{bucket}/{userId}/{projectId}/{trackId}/{clipId}.wav`
- **Formats:** Accept WAV, FLAC, MP3, OGG; transcode to WAV internally for editing

**Data model:**
```sql
CREATE TABLE audio_files (
    id          UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    user_id     UUID REFERENCES users(id),
    project_id  UUID REFERENCES projects(id),
    filename    VARCHAR(255),
    s3_key      TEXT NOT NULL,
    size_bytes  BIGINT,
    duration_ms INT,
    sample_rate INT,
    channels    INT,
    format      VARCHAR(10),
    waveform    JSONB,  -- pre-computed peaks for rendering
    created_at  TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

