### 3.4 Browser DAW Editor

The editor is the heart of the application — a Canvas/WebGL rendered multi-track timeline.

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph Editor Components
        TL["Timeline (Canvas)"]
        TR["Track List (React)"]
        MX["Mixer Panel (React)"]
        PI["Piano Roll (Canvas)"]
        TB["Transport Bar (React)"]
        PL["Plugin Rack (React)"]
        BR["Browser Panel (React)"]
    end

    subgraph State Management
        ZS["Zustand Store"]
        UH["Undo/Redo History"]
        IDB["IndexedDB Snapshot"]
    end

    TL --> ZS
    TR --> ZS
    MX --> ZS
    PI --> ZS
    TB --> ZS
    ZS --> UH
    ZS --> IDB
```

**Key components:**

| Component | Technology | Responsibility |
|-----------|-----------|----------------|
| **Timeline** | HTML Canvas | Waveform rendering, clip placement, selection, scrubbing |
| **Track List** | React + Tailwind | Track controls: name, color, mute/solo, volume/pan |
| **Mixer Panel** | React + WebGL meters | Channel strips, VU meters, send routing |
| **Piano Roll** | HTML Canvas | MIDI note editing, velocity, CC lanes |
| **Transport Bar** | React | Play/pause/stop/record, BPM, time signature, metronome |
| **Plugin Rack** | React | Insert/send effects chain per track |
| **Browser Panel** | React | File browser, sample library, instrument presets |

**State architecture (Zustand store slices):**

```typescript
interface DAWState {
  // Transport
  isPlaying: boolean;
  isRecording: boolean;
  currentTime: number;    // in beats
  bpm: number;
  timeSignature: [number, number];
  loopEnabled: boolean;
  loopStart: number;
  loopEnd: number;

  // Tracks & Clips
  tracks: Track[];
  clips: Clip[];
  selectedClipIds: string[];
  selectedTrackId: string | null;

  // Mixer
  masterVolume: number;
  soloedTrackIds: string[];

  // Editor
  zoom: number;           // pixels per beat
  scrollX: number;
  scrollY: number;
  snapToGrid: boolean;
  gridResolution: number; // 1 = quarter note

  // Undo
  undoStack: DAWSnapshot[];
  redoStack: DAWSnapshot[];

  // Actions
  addTrack: (type: TrackType) => void;
  removeTrack: (id: string) => void;
  addClip: (trackId: string, clip: Clip) => void;
  moveClip: (clipId: string, newStart: number, newTrackId?: string) => void;
  splitClip: (clipId: string, atTime: number) => void;
  undo: () => void;
  redo: () => void;
}
```

