### 3.5 Real-Time Audio Engine

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph Audio Thread ["Audio Thread (AudioWorklet)"]
        MIX["Mixer Worklet"]
        FX1["Effect Worklet (EQ)"]
        FX2["Effect Worklet (Compressor)"]
        FX3["Effect Worklet (Reverb)"]
    end

    subgraph Main Thread
        SCH["Scheduler"]
        BUF["Buffer Manager"]
        DEC["Decoder (OfflineAudioContext)"]
    end

    SCH -->|schedule clips| MIX
    BUF -->|decoded PCM| MIX
    MIX --> FX1 --> FX2 --> FX3
    FX3 --> OUT["AudioContext.destination"]
```

**Architecture:**

1. **AudioContext** — Single shared context per project session
2. **Scheduler** — Lookahead scheduler (25ms intervals, 100ms lookahead) for sample-accurate timing
3. **Buffer Manager** — Caches decoded `AudioBuffer` objects, lazy-loads from IndexedDB/S3
4. **AudioWorklet processors:**
   - `mixer-processor.js` — Summing, panning, gain per track
   - `metering-processor.js` — RMS/peak level metering at 60fps
   - `effects/*.js` — EQ, compressor, delay, reverb, chorus
5. **Clip playback:** `AudioBufferSourceNode` per clip, scheduled via `start(when, offset, duration)`

**Latency targets:**
- Playback latency: < 20ms (128 sample buffer @ 44.1kHz)
- Visual sync: requestAnimationFrame tied to `audioContext.currentTime`

**Key code pattern — lookahead scheduler:**
```typescript
class AudioScheduler {
  private scheduleAheadTime = 0.1;  // 100ms
  private timerInterval = 25;       // ms

  start() {
    this.timerID = setInterval(() => this.schedule(), this.timerInterval);
  }

  private schedule() {
    const currentTime = this.audioContext.currentTime;
    const lookAhead = currentTime + this.scheduleAheadTime;

    for (const clip of this.activeClips) {
      const clipStartSec = this.beatsToSeconds(clip.startTime);
      if (clipStartSec < lookAhead && !clip.isScheduled) {
        this.scheduleClip(clip, clipStartSec);
        clip.isScheduled = true;
      }
    }
  }
}
```

